                "height": 768,
                "alt": "Grainy greyscale radio image: one small, bright, slightly stretched smudge in the middle of a dark speckled field.",
                "caption": "Haumea's own heat at a wavelength of 0.87 mm, from five sessions between 6 and 23 July 2023 added together. North is up and the picture is 0.31 arcseconds across. Hubble, Webb and Keck see Haumea as a point; here it spans about three times the finest detail ALMA could make out. The ring these observations were looking for cannot be made out.",
